ed-cross-and-red-crescent-societies", "targetName": "International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies", "context": "The IFRC collaborates with various charity organizations to enhance the efficiency and reach of humanitarian efforts globally."}, {"sourceSlug": "geneva-switzerland", "sourceName": "Geneva, Switzerland", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "international-federation-of-red-cross-and-red-crescent-societies", "targetName": "International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies", "context": "The IFRC is headquartered in Geneva, Switzerland, where it coordinates global humanitarian initiatives."}], "places": [{"name": "Geneva, Switzerland", "role": "Headquarters"}, {"name": "Paris, France", "role": "Key Conference Site"}, {"name": "New York City, USA", "role": "Major Collaborative Hub"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "international-federation-of-red-cross-and-red-crescent-societies"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1069175", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Federation_of_Red_Cross_and_Red_Crescent_Societies"], "tags": ["Switzerland", "nonprofit organization", "Europe", "Humanitarian & Relief Organizations", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies contributed to the historical record of the Modern period. Key lasting impacts include: Shaped institutional landscape and community development. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "The IFRC has shaped humanitarian response on a global scale, influencing the establishment of laws and protocols that govern international aid, impacting millions of lives since its inception.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T20:54:28Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#29956813591", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Humanitarian organization. International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies is a nonprofit organization in Geneva, established in 1919. A moderately significant entity in the historical record. Relevant to cause-and-effect analysis.", "newValue": "The International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies (IFRC), founded in 1919 in Geneva, Switzerland, stands as a pivotal institution in humanitarian efforts and international relief frameworks. The IFRC emerged in the aftermath of World War I, a conflict that underscored the need for organized humanitarian response to the suffering of war victims across Europe and beyond. Its establishment marked a significant evolution in how nations and societies coordinate disaster relief, medical aid, and emergency services, laying the groundwork for future humanitarian laws and principles.

In its early years, the IFRC played a crucial role in providing assistance to war-torn regions and establishing standards for humanitarian action. By 1921, it had convened its first International Conference, bringing together national Red Cross societies to share best practices and coordinate efforts. The organization was instrumental in the adoption of the Geneva Conventions, which set international legal standards for humanitarian treatment in war. Over the decades, the IFRC has expanded its reach, providing aid during natural disasters and health crises, such as the 2004 Indian Ocean tsunami and the ongoing challenges posed by the COVID-19 pandemic.

The legacy of the IFRC is evident in its influence on global humanitarian standards and the establishment of the International Humanitarian Law framework. It has inspired numerous organizations worldwide, fostering an ethos of volunteerism and altruism that persists today. The IFRC's commitment to neutrality, impartiality, and independence continues to shape humanitarian responses, pushing forward the idea that all individuals deserve assistance regardless of nationality or political affiliations."}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-22T20:54:28Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#29956813591", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": ["Organizational need and institutional development"], "newValue": ["The devastation of World War I created an urgent need for coordinated humanitarian assistance.", "The establishment of the Geneva Conventions laid the groundwork for international humanitarian law.", "The proliferation of national Red Cross societies in the 19th century provided a framework for international collaboration on humanitarian issues."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-22T20:54:28Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#29956813591", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": ["Shaped institutional landscape and community development"], "newValue": ["The IFRC has set global standards for humanitarian response and disaster relief efforts.", "It has influenced the creation of numerous humanitarian organizations worldwide, expanding the reach of aid.", "The organization has contributed to the development and enforcement of international humanitarian law."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-22T20:54:28Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#29956813591", "field": "detailsJson.relationships", "oldValue": [{"sourceSlug": "international-federation-of-red-cross-and-red-crescent-societies", "sourceName": "International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "era-interwar-period", "targetName": "Interwar Period", "context": "International Fede